# A block named by the former spelling `var` is no data of a launch (the author 2026-11-11: the special name is
# `data`): in the code of Code its head `var` is an ordinary name, which the launch does not find -- answer 3 at the
# call.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call
# main(). The block stays a child of Code on purpose: written apart, the launch would have nothing to refuse.
sub: main () (
    Code:
        var(int: x 1)
        x := x + 1
)
    call: Code\var Code
main()
int: seen main\data\Code\var\x
